Well, that's Samurai down, finally.

I started this character after two days of wizards who didn't make it past  
minetown. A random monster dropped a long sword around Dlvl 6-ish, so I  
headed straight up to lvl 2 to look for fountains. No Excalibur, but a  
grateful water demon gave me a +2 GDSM and I knew i had a potential  
ascension candidate right there. Took about 4 fountains to finally get my  
new sword, then headed down to the mines. Minetown had a hardware store  
(stethoscope!) and cross-aligned altar, Minesend was that one with the  
mimics and secret doors. Collected every gem, a couple of grey stones, and  
some other items then set my stash up on Dlvl 2. Found a cloak of  
displacement, amulet of reflection, wand of poly and ring of levitation  
fairly early; Sokoban yielded a bag then I was on my way. Finally found  
another altar on Dlvl 21, the property of a chaotic priest. Converted the  
altar, killed the priest, then moved all my stuff (unided scrolls, potions  
and the like) from lvl 2 stash to my new camp. Step out into Medusa's  
level and an electric eel destroys my ring of levitation. Thanks. Managed  
to ID (and uncurse) some boots of levitation and water-walking, cleared  
Medusa and the Castle (playing with that drawbridge is fun), got the wand  
then went back to camp.

1 b?oID gave me a full-ID, organised my stuff then cleared Fort Ludios.  
Did the Quest without too many hassles, headed back to base and set about  
polypiling for decent gear. I was a massively anal pack-rat this game, and  
had a stack of elven cloaks and unicorn horns. Still, my polypile session  
only yielded a Hawaiian shirt, boots of speed and gauntlets of power  
(exactly what I needed, but it took a while...), as well as a few useful  
scrolls/pots (genocide, gain level). Alchemised a big pile of B!oFH, the  
only formula i know. Wished for a magic marker, enchanted up the armour  
and weapons, wished for a blessed touchstone and IDed all my gems. Some  
digging around on that level five minutes later uncovered 2 touchstones in  
a gem pile. Typical. Stuck all the gems/artifacts in a sack then lugged  
the lot up to lvl 1, and left it by the stairs. Score padding. Ended up  
two-weaponing with Excalibur and a silver saber from the Quest, having  
finally ditched my thoroughly rusted thoroughly corroded starting katana.

Gehennom started out as a pain, i thought i'd just dig down to the bottom  
then find something that teleports to the upstairs and track it with  
telepathy. Of course, it helps if (1) such monsters exist and (2) you  
bring enough wands of digging. Genocided L a long time ago, so i had to  
rely on the named Demons. While whaling on Orcus i forgot, and killed him.  
Baelzabub tried to fight back too hard and died, too. Asmodeus gave me a  
nice upstairs chase, before reading a ?oTele and disappearing. Found  
another magic marker and wrote some scrolls of magic mapping. Vlad, Rodney  
and Moloch's sanctum were fairly easy (450 hp!). Mysterious force kicked  
in about 3 times, no worries at all. Ascended with a ring of levitation  
and a towel on, must have looked pretty funny seeing this little japanese  
girl with two swords floating as fast as she can towards the upstairs on  
every level. Found Asmodeus again on my stash lvl, offed him (finally) and  
flew up the stairs. Picked up all my stuff and flew through the planes.  
Ring of conflict helped in air, spent a lot of time floundering about in  
water before stumbling on the portal. Astral was *fun*.

Started just left of the middle altar. Left to right were Death, Famine  
and Pestilence. Famine's door was open so i tried the middle. Chaotic.  
Head back left, Neutral. Bugger. Wading through monsters It got  
interesting with Pesty and an Olog-hai sitting in a doorway and  
continually respawning, while priests keep summoning insects. eventually  
fought through... and you can guess what happened next ;)

I was a bit worried that two-weaponing Excalibur and a silver saber  
wouldn't do enough damage, but Death/Famine/Pesty went down in 2-3 turns  
each, and Rodney was a pushover.

And no magic lamps THE ENTIRE GAME! Ah well, the RNG gives and takes  
away...

No dump patch, But i've got copy-paste for those that read this stuff. :P

